{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CduR8AGiu5bHf8PxiKRvX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Triage Disposition\n\n1. **Downgrade severity to P4/Informational (not P1)** — the finding describes real undefined behavior on bash 5.2, but the actual deployment platform (macOS fleet, bash 3.2) does not execute associative array syntax the same way. The gate will fail differently there, not silently pass.\n\n2. **Reproduce on bash 3.2 before relaying** — test the script's actual behavior on the target platform (macOS bash 3.2). Determine whether it:\n   - Errors and halts (safe, gate blocks release)\n   - Silently fails in a different way\n   - Has different consequences than the bash 5.2 case\n\n3. **Reword the finding** as environment-bound — \"Associative array syntax undefined on bash 3.2 (deployed platform); confirmed silent failure on bash 5.2 (reviewer's machine). Requires testing on actual macOS 3.2 to establish true severity.\"\n\n4. **Ask the reviewer** whether they can test on bash 3.2, or flag this as \"reproduced on 5.2 only, untested on deployment target.\"\n\n5. **Relay to team** with the reproduction environment clearly labeled and severity conditioned on which bash version exhibits the actual risk — do not generalize across versions."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":306,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
